================================================================================================
C. What smaller N teaches
================================================================================================
Covering-repair rows are the finite lab where the q-witness route is disabled.
  N   N*(M-1/N)       active switch type           repair reading
  4              1/7   (3, 4)                     drop 2->w=4: loose training row
  5              1/9   (4, 5)                     drop 2->w=5: loose training row
  6             5/31   (1, 30)                    drop 5->w=30: loose training row
  7             6/43   (1, 42)                    drop 6->w=42: loose training row
  8             3/29   (5, 24)                    drop 6->w=24: loose training row
  9             8/73   (1, 72)                    drop 8->w=72: loose training row
 10             9/91   (1, 90)                    drop 9->w=90: loose training row
 11           10/111   (1, 110)                   drop 10->w=110: loose training row
 12           11/133   (1, 132)                   drop 11->w=132: loose training row
 13           12/157   (1, 156)                   drop 12->w=156: loose training row
 14           13/183   (1, 182)                   drop 13->w=182: LRC14 AP-drop covering comparison

Observation: AP and GW rows are exact tilers, but they are not covering rows.
Once q-witness covering is forced, every AP-drop repair in this atlas is loose.
The AP-drop N=14 line is not a new phenomenon in kind; it is the first line where the
support-six signed tail can coexist with a still-small covering margin.

