N=12: q=6, support floor=5, below support-six
N=14: q=7, support floor=6, first support-six

================================================================================================
Tournament Analysis
================================================================================================
Vertices are proof carriers rather than runners.
Observable: how much LRC proof structure survives before scalarizing.
Hamiltonian path:
  q_witness_covering_reduction > binding_pair_covering_margin > AP_tight_equal_spacing > Goddyn_Wong_acceleration_atom > support_floor_q_minus_1 > raw_speed_search
Challenged assumption: below-14 proof should be learned from raw finite
enumeration.  The useful training objects are q-cover deficits, binding
switches, acceleration windows, and the support floor.
